<div class="eyebrow">AJSMR POLICY</div><h1>Research Ethics, Consent &amp; Clinical/Animal Research</h1><section><h2>General Principle</h2><p>Research published by AJSMR must comply with applicable ethical, legal and institutional requirements and internationally accepted standards for responsible research.</p></section><section><h2>Human Research</h2><p>Manuscripts involving human participants should identify the approving ethics committee or institutional review body and approval or reference number where applicable.</p></section><section><h2>Informed Consent</h2><p>Where identifiable information, photographs, clinical details or other potentially identifying material is published, appropriate consent for publication should be obtained.</p></section><section><h2>Animal Research</h2><p>Research involving animals must include an ethics or animal-use statement identifying the relevant oversight body and confirming compliance with applicable animal-welfare requirements.</p></section><section><h2>Clinical Research</h2><p>Clinical studies should identify applicable registration details where registration is required or appropriate and report methods and outcomes transparently.</p></section>
